==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|upheven|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|ūphebban}}, {{m|ang|ūpāhebban||to lift up, raise up, exalt, rise in the air, fly}}, equivalent to {{prefix|up|heave|lang=en}}. Cognate with {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|opheffen||to lift, raise|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|aufheben||to lift, raise, cancel, repeal|lang=de}}.

===Verb===
{{en-verb|upheaves|upheaving|upheaved|past2=uphove|upheaved|past_ptc2=uphoven}} (''transitive'' or ''intransitive'')

# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To [[heave]] or [[lift]] up; [[raise]] up or [[aloft]].
# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To [[lift]] or [[thrust]] something [[upward]] [[forcefully]], or be similarly lifted or thrust upward.
# {{context|intransitive|lang=en}} To be lifted up; [[rise]].

